const densityNarrative = {
  eyebrow: 'REPAIR IN CLOSE QUARTERS',
  headline: 'What Condos and Townhomes Change About the Job',
  paragraphs: [
    "A washer leak in a detached house ruins a floor. The same leak on the third level of a condo building ruins three ceilings, a neighbor's weekend, and the HOA's patience — which is why dense-housing calls get treated with a different urgency and a different checklist. Water connections get inspected along with the machine itself; drain pans and shut-offs get verified while the panel is off; and the stacked pairs that live in ventilation-starved closets get their airflow checked, because a dryer breathing through a crushed duct in a closet works harder and dies younger.",
    "Compact machines are their own specialty. The 24-inch stacked pairs, the 18-inch dishwashers in older complexes, the counter-depth refrigerators chosen to fit a galley kitchen — they're not shrunken versions of full-size machines; they're different platforms with different parts, and a truck stocked only for suburban full-size kitchens shows up empty-handed. Ours isn't.",
    "And access is half the job: gate codes, elevator reservations, parking that doesn't block the fire lane, work hours the CC&Rs allow. We collect that once, keep it on the account, and show up the second time already knowing the drill. Buildings remember contractors who respect the building — it's the cheapest reputation there is."
  ]
};

const hoaNarrative = {
  eyebrow: 'FOR BOARDS & PROPERTY MANAGERS',
  headline: 'The Paperwork Is Part of the Repair',
  paragraphs: [
    "Solana Beach runs on associations, and associations run on documentation. So the workflow we bring to managed buildings is built around it: a written estimate before work starts, itemized so a board can approve it by email; proof of our BHGS registration and insurance on file with the management company, not re-requested per job; an invoice afterward that states what failed, what was replaced, and what's warrantied — the kind that survives an audit or a homeowner dispute without a phone call.",
